<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mtext>â€…â€Š</mtext><mo>â‰ˆ</mo><mtext>â€…â€Š</mtext><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>Î±</mi><mtext>â€‰</mtext><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Î”</mi><mi>H</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="script">M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C(X) \;\approx\; 1 + \alpha \,\frac{\Delta H}{H(\mathcal{M})}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.07153em;">C</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.07847em;">X</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">â‰ˆ</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.7278em; vertical-align: -0.0833em;"></span><span class="mord">1</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">+</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1.3923em; vertical-align: -0.52em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.0037em;">Î±</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mopen nulldelimiter"></span><span class="mfrac"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.8723em;"><span style="top: -2.655em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.08125em;">H</span><span class="mopen mtight">(</span><span class="mord mathcal mtight">M</span><span class="mclose mtight">)</span></span></span></span><span style="top: -3.23em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span class="frac-line" style="border-bottom-width: 0.04em;"></span></span><span style="top: -3.394em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mtight">Î”</span><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.08125em;">H</span></span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">â€‹</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.52em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mclose nulldelimiter"></span></span></span></span></span></p>
<h4 dir="auto" class="">5) Reuse, Parallelism, Degeneracy as Information Discounts</h4>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Treat these as code-length discounts relative to the raw assembly plan.</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Reuse: library motifs shorten description. If motif dictionary has description amortized across instances, the effective bits per instance drop. Model as a divisor on <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A(X)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">A</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.07847em;">X</span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span>.</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Parallelism: independent sub-assemblies compress as a product code; wall-clock and effective complexity per unit time fall. Model as a divisor on <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A(X)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">A</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.07847em;">X</span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span>.</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Degeneracy: if many alternatives achieve the same function, the description of â€œa solutionâ€ is shorter than â€œthis specific solution.â€ Function-first coding reduces effective complexity; model as a divisor.</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">This aligns the original formula with MDL-style accounting: EAIMR rises when, despite these discounts, the remaining coordinated specification is still large and functionally tight.</p>
<h4 dir="auto" class="">6) Coherence via Control &amp; Causal Graphs</h4>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Let <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G(X)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">G</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.07847em;">X</span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span> be a causal graph extracted from <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.07847em;">X</span></span></span></span>'s dynamics. Define a control coherence term:</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>Ï•</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mtext>â€…â€Š</mtext><mo>=</mo><mtext>â€…â€Š</mtext><msub><mi>Î²</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mtext>â€‰</mtext><mtext>Stab</mtext><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mtext>â€…â€Š</mtext><mo>+</mo><mtext>â€…â€Š</mtext><msub><mi>Î²</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mtext>â€‰</mtext><mtext>GoalAcc</mtext><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mtext>â€…â€Š</mtext><mo>+</mo><mtext>â€…â€Š</mtext><msub><mi>Î²</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mtext>â€‰</mtext><mtext>Robust</mtext><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi(X) \;=\; \beta_1\, \text{Stab}(G) \;+\; \beta_2\, \text{GoalAcc}(G) \;+\; \beta_3\, \text{Robust}(G)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">Ï•</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.07847em;">X</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05278em;">Î²</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3011em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0528em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">1</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">â€‹</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">Stab</span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">G</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">+</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05278em;">Î²</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3011em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0528em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">2</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">â€‹</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">GoalAcc</span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">G</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">+</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05278em;">Î²</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3011em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0528em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">3</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">â€‹</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">Robust</span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">G</span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span></p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mtext>GoalAcc</mtext><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{GoalAcc}(G)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">GoalAcc</span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">G</span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span>: accuracy tracking a specified functional setpoint (e.g., temperature band in termite mounds).</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mtext>Robust</mtext><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Robust}(G)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">Robust</span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">G</span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span>: performance under noise/lesions (graceful degradation).</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Then use <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>Ï•</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi(X)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">Ï•</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.07847em;">X</span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span> inside (Section 3) or directly as the coherence multiplier.</p>
<h4 dir="auto" class="">7) Practical Estimation (finite data)</h4>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Because <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K(X)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.07153em;">K</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.07847em;">X</span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span> is uncomputable, rely on approximations:</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Compression proxies: on suitable encodings (graphs, fields, symbol streams).</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Surprisal under null: fit <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_0</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8333em; vertical-align: -0.15em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.13889em;">P</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3011em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.1389em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">0</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">â€‹</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> (e.g., generative physics sims, random graphs) and estimate by Monte Carlo or density models.</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Function &amp; coherence: quantify with control/evaluation tasks (tracking error, energy efficiency, resilience curves).</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Discounts: measure from libraries (motif counts), concurrency (critical path vs. total ops), and function-equivalence classes (number of viable variants).</p>
<h4 dir="auto" class="">8) Worked Intuitions (triad examples)</h4>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Neural tissue: very high <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A(X)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">A</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.07847em;">X</span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span> (precise mesoscale organization), strong <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C(X)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.07153em;">C</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.07847em;">X</span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span> (robust goal pursuit), discounts present (columns, parallelism), yet EAIMR stays high mind-like.</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Termite mound: moderate <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A(X)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">A</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.07847em;">X</span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span> vs. dunes, high <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C(X)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.07153em;">C</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.07847em;">X</span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span> (thermoregulation), sizable discounts (motifs, parallel labor, many workable designs) but coordinated control keeps EAIMR high.</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Forest: extremely high macro <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A(X)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">A</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.07847em;">X</span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span> vs. random vegetation, high robustness/goal achievement (nutrient routing, succession), massive reuse/degeneracy, yet coherence over centuries pushes EAIMR high.</p>
<h4 dir="auto" class="">9) Decision Rule (operational)</h4>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Define thresholds from a reference set of clearly mindless assemblies:</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mtext>EAIMR</mtext><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mtext>â€…â€Š</mtext><mo>â‰¥</mo><mtext>â€…â€Š</mtext><mi>Ï„</mi><mtext>â€…â€Š</mtext><mtext>â€…â€Š</mtext><mo>â‡’</mo><mtext>â€…â€Š</mtext><mtext>â€…â€Š</mtext><mtext>classify&nbsp;as&nbsp;mind-like&nbsp;(candidate)</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{EAIMR}(X) \;\ge\; \tau \;\;\Rightarrow\;\; \text{classify as mind-like (candidate)}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">EAIMR</span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.07847em;">X</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">â‰¥</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.4306em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.1132em;">Ï„</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">â‡’</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">classify&nbsp;as&nbsp;mind-like&nbsp;(candidate)</span></span>