Would you like me to expand this into a parallel argument structure (plants/animals â†” cognitive minorities â†” AI systems), so itâ€™s crystal clear that the same bias underlies all three cases of exclusion? Right â€” Michael Levinâ€™s work really strengthens your point. He uses â€œmind blindnessâ€ to describe how humans systematically fail to recognize intelligence in non-human systems â€” especially in animals, plants, and even cellular collectives.
&nbsp;
Levinâ€™s core claim: intelligence is not limited to brains; itâ€™s any system that can pursue goals, adapt to perturbations, and solve problems in its own medium. Cells in a regenerating limb, for example, show agency in shaping growth.
