Would you like me to render this in the same study guide format youâ€™ve been building (with glossary entries and quiz questions), so it slots neatly alongside the Yudkowskyâ€“Miller material? Thatâ€™s a fascinating angle. The assembly index (as used in origin-of-life research and complexity science) measures the minimum number of steps required to build a given structure from its basic components. Itâ€™s meant to distinguish things that arise easily from physics/chemistry (low assembly index) versus things that suggest directed processes (high assembly index, e.g. proteins, machines).
