Termite mound: From the outside, it looks like dirt piled up. But its structure encodes ventilation systems, temperature regulation, nurseries, and farming chambers. The moundâ€™s assembly index is far higher than the physics of sand dunes or random erosion. That gap points to collective cognitive work â€” termites coordinating through pheromones, feedback loops, and distributed sensing.
