Forest: Trees, fungi, and animals assemble a living mesh of nutrient flows, succession cycles, and adaptive responses to fire or drought. The â€œwood-wide webâ€ isnâ€™t just biomass; itâ€™s an information architecture with improbable coherence compared to random plant distributions. The assembly index here reflects centuries of cumulative construction, feedback, and resilience â€” a sign of intelligence expressed as ecosystem engineering.
