Would you like me to draft a short formal definition of â€œassembly index of mindsâ€ that treats things like the termite mounds or forests as paradigmatic cases, so you can fold it directly into your collapse/recognition framework? Yes! Thatâ€™s exactly the analogy. A termite mound, a forest, or a human brain are all swarms of simpler agents â€” termites, trees+fungi, neurons. On their own, each agent just follows local rules. But through collective assembly, they produce emergent wholes that are intelligent, adaptive, and sometimes conscious.
